{
  "id": "2219cca3-9ed4-4708-9e4c-bc480faad753",
  "featureId": "ebb9ceb0-ea12-4374-af6e-12aa4256bcc3",
  "number": 80,
  "shortId": "6TMUZ",
  "priority": 18,
  "slug": "plugin-10-keybinding-command-palette-integration-for-contributed-actions",
  "title": "plugin-10: Keybinding + command-palette integration for contributed actions",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "A provider or plugin can register an action, but nothing binds it to a key from config or shows it in the command palette. The plan's Phase 11 half that has no phase.",
  "description": "Added 2026-07-26 after auditing docs/chrome-and-ui.md against the planner. This is the\nhalf of the plan's \"Phase 11 — Config / Keybinding / Command Palette Integration\" that no phase\ncovers. F003/P007 (plugin-09) covers the CONFIG half. F003/P013 (menu-nav) is about navigating\ninside a list or menu, which is a different thing entirely.\n\n═══ WHAT ALREADY EXISTS — BUILD ON IT, DO NOT REINVENT ═══\nThe action side is DONE (F003/P003, plugin-04):\n- `ActionRegistry` + `ActionCatalog` (`heca/src/actions.rs`) — one runtime registry. A name-keyed\n  action registers through `register_dynamic(registry, catalog, meta, handler)`.\n- `ActionMeta` carries `name`, `label`, `description`, `category`, `default_binding`, `icon`,\n  `policy`, and an optional `confirm`. **`default_binding` already exists on the metadata** — that\n  is the hook this phase consumes.\n- `ActionCatalog::describe_all()` / `describe(name)` → `ActionInfo` (serde). Introspection is\n  already there, which is what a palette needs to list things.\n- `unregister_dynamic` + an RAII `ActionHandle`, so a contributed action disappears when its\n  provider unmounts.\n\n═══ WHAT IS MISSING ═══\n- A contributed action's `default_binding` is never read by the keymap. Registering an action does\n  not make a key work.\n- `keybindings.default.toml` and the user's keybindings only speak to built-in `WmAction`s. There\n  is no path for a user to bind a provider's or plugin's action by name.\n- The command palette does not list contributed actions. It should, since `describe_all()` already\n  returns them.\n- Nothing resolves a collision between a contributed default binding and an existing one, and\n  nothing tells the user when a contributed binding is refused.\n\n═══ WORK ═══\n1. Read `default_binding` from `ActionMeta` when an action registers, and offer it to the keymap.\n2. Let a user bind ANY action by name in config, contributed ones included — the same syntax as a\n   built-in. The registry is keyed by name already, so this is a lookup, not a new mechanism.\n3. Feed the palette from `ActionCatalog::describe_all()` so contributed actions are listed,\n   searchable and runnable, with their label, icon and category.\n4. Decide collision behaviour with the user: does a contributed default lose to an existing\n   binding, or win? Whatever is chosen, the user must be TOLD, not silently ignored — the\n   Improvements feature (F010) already covers notifying about blocked keybindings.\n5. Honour `ActionPolicy` at dispatch, exactly as a built-in does. A contributed action must not\n   bypass the policy system.\n6. Unbinding on unmount: when a provider goes away its bindings must go with it, through the\n   existing RAII handle.\n\n═══ RULES THAT APPLY ═══\n- Input parity (AGENTS.md, grid-ui plan P2): an action reachable from the palette must also be\n  bindable and reachable over RPC. All three or none.\n- Never hardcode a binding. It goes through `KeymapRegistry` like everything else.\n- Follow the full Adding-New-Actions checklist in AGENTS.md for anything new this phase adds.\n\n═══ DEPENDS ON ═══\nF003/P003 (done) for the registry. Best done alongside or after F003/P009 (config-file plugins),\nwhich is the other half of the plan's Phase 11 and will produce contributed actions to bind.",
