      "shortId": "MV7N5",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "realize-coverage",
      "title": "viewnode-task-1: Complete realize coverage",
      "status": "canceled",
      "description": "Complete `realize` coverage in `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs`. Missing `WidgetKind` arms: `Select`, `Tabs`, `Grid`, `ItemGroup`, `DockFrame`, `MarkerGroup`, `ScrollBar`, `Toast` (was `plugin-task-ui-9`). Each arm: build the heca-grid-ui widget from `ViewNode` props resolved against `Theme`, wire events to `Intent`s, recurse children, attach via `.child(...)` (or `*_boxed` setters for body subtrees).\n\nCurrent state: `realize.rs` covers the basic containers + leaf widgets but these structured-prop widgets still lack a `realize` arm — they cannot be authored declaratively via `ViewNode` (plugins/RPC/modal bodies) yet.\n\nBehaviors to preserve: existing arms unchanged; `WidgetKind` closed vocabulary; props are semantic (`ViewVariant`/`ViewSize`/`ViewAlign` + Glyph/color names) resolved by the host; `Intent`-based events stay serializable. Add showcase coverage + `docs/widgets.md` + rustdoc for each new arm.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "c9937902-a2bd-4ed3-8115-551bf87a7396-check-001-in-progress-canceled",
          "date": "2026-07-13T20:48:19.980Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "canceled",
          "title": "SUPERSEDED by phase `viewnode-choice` (1df9c36c, 8 tasks: choice-1..8) — created 2026-07-13 with the user.",
          "description": "SUPERSEDED by phase `viewnode-choice` (1df9c36c, 8 tasks: choice-1..8) — created 2026-07-13 with the user.\n\nThis task assumed the 8 missing kinds only needed *structured props*. Investigation showed that is wrong: they split into three different gaps, and the option-shaped ones need a **widget refactor**, not a prop. `Select` (`select.rs:77`) and `Tabs` (`tabs.rs:51`) are **self-contained** — they hand-draw their options/segments and hit-test by arithmetic, with no child components — so they violate the standing composition rule and must be refactored the way `Button` was (`07d4c1a`, PR #237).\n\nThe user also chose a better model than a `props[\"options\"]` string list: an option is a **node with a value and arbitrary content**, and options are **children** — a new `Choice` primitive (`<option value=…>` / SwiftUI `.tag()`), reused by `Select`, `Tabs`, and later `ContextMenu`/`CommandPalette`. `Choice` and `Item` coexist (documented guidance in choice-8).\n\nAll of this task's scope is carried by the new phase: `Select`/`Tabs` (choice-2/3/4), `ItemGroup`/`MarkerGroup` (choice-5), `Grid` + `PropValue::List` (choice-6), `DockFrame`/`Toast` + named slots (choice-7), `ScrollBar` documented host-only + a coverage guard test (choice-8)."
        }
      ],
