    {
      "id": "23d2e8b8-e251-4ae5-9f74-cd28ae96ff4b",
      "phaseId": "68a01ad8-1026-4c09-b516-2e2838723903",
      "number": 277,
      "shortId": "AUFAE",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "viewnode-task-3-exhaustive-wid",
      "title": "viewnode-task-3: Exhaustive widget docs for the composition changes (both audiences)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Complete `docs/widgets.md` for everything `viewnode-task-2` (commit `07d4c1a`, PR #237) introduced, to the standard AGENTS.md now mandates: **every** builder/prop/event/signal documented, with **runnable code examples for BOTH audiences** — the native builder API *and* the declarative `ViewNode` form — including precedence rules.\n\n## Current state (what `viewnode-task-2` already documented)\n- `### Button` — rewritten: content-is-children, sugar vs composed, size hugging, inherited content color, one-Tab-stop; native + `ViewNode` examples incl. the children-win precedence.\n- `### Item` — composition note (label is a `Label` child; state color inherited; active-bold via signal; `focus_barrier`).\n- `#### Base` table — new `focus_barrier` row.\n- `PaintCx` table — `with_content_color` / `content_color` rows.\n- `### Size variants` — the variant now cascades down the tree (`Style::size_explicit` / `Style::set_size`).\n\n## Gaps to close (this task)\n1. **`### Label`** (`docs/widgets.md:611`) — document the new `bold_signal()` accessor and that **color is inherited when unset** (falls back to `cx.content_color()`, then theme foreground; an explicit `.color()` opts out). Add the `ViewNode` form (`WidgetKind::Label`, prop `text`).\n2. **`### Icon`** — same inheritance note (primary layer falls back to the inherited content color), plus its `ViewNode` form (`WidgetKind::Icon`, prop `icon` = Glyph **name**).\n3. **`### Item`** — add the declarative example (`WidgetKind::Item`: prop `text`, event `press`) and state plainly that its slots/children are **not** yet modelled in `ViewNode` (needs structured/named children — belongs to `viewnode-task-1`).\n4. **Declarative UI model table** (`docs/widgets.md:1710`) — the `Button` row must now read `text`, `icon`, `variant`, `size` **+ children**, and the section must state the **precedence: children win; the scalar props are the childless sugar**.\n5. **A single side-by-side \"both ways\" Button example** near the Button entry, so the two spellings and their identical outcome are visible at a glance (the user asked for this explicitly).\n\n## Files\n`docs/widgets.md` only (rustdoc already landed in `07d4c1a`). Cross-check against `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/{button,item,label,icon}.rs`, `heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs` (`Base.focus_barrier`, `PaintCx::with_content_color`), `heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs` (`size_explicit`/`set_size`), `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs` (`realize_button` precedence + `glyph_from_name`).\n\n## Edge cases\n- Do not document props `realize` does not actually read (the model is untrusted input; realize is total and ignores unknown/mistyped props).\n- Keep the `Not realized yet` list accurate (`Select`/`Tabs`/`Grid`/`ItemGroup`/`DockFrame`/`MarkerGroup`/`ScrollBar`/`Toast`).\n- Ships on the existing PR branch `feat/viewnode-button-composition` (PR #237) as a follow-up commit.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-13 — commit `cbada04`, pushed to `feat/viewnode-button-composition` (PR #237).\n\n## Shipped in `docs/widgets.md`\n1. **`### Button` → new subsection \"The two ways to build a Button — same widget, same retained tree\"**: a 3-row matrix (simple / simple+icon / composed × native builder vs declarative `ViewNode`) plus four runnable, commented examples — simple native, simple declarative (childless sugar), composed native (arbitrary tree), composed declarative (identical tree as data). Ends with the **precedence rule: children win; the scalar props are the childless sugar** — one content model, two spellings, never two paint paths.\n2. **`### Label`**: added `bold_signal()` accessor (re-weight in place; how `Item` bolds while active, since the inherited paint context carries a color but not a weight) + **color is inherited when unset** (`cx.content_color()` → `theme.foreground`; explicit `.color()` opts out) + `ViewNode` form.\n3. **`### Icon`**: same inheritance for the primary layer (secondary follows it); clarified `.size(px)` is **glyph pixels**, NOT the `WidgetSize` variant (use `Style::set_size`, since `size` is taken) + `ViewNode` form + glyph-name resolution (unknown name → no icon, never a panic).\n4. **`### Item`**: `ViewNode` form (prop `text`, event `press`) + an explicit statement that its **slots are not modelled declaratively yet** (needs *named* children in the model → `viewnode-task-1`); native code composes them freely today.\n5. **Declarative model table**: `Button` row split out — now reads `variant`, `size`, **+ children (the content)**, with `text`/`icon` as the childless sugar; added a callout above the table pointing at the Button section.\n\n(The Base `focus_barrier` row, the `PaintCx::with_content_color`/`content_color` rows and the size-variant cascade were already documented in `07d4c1a`.)\n\n## Gates\nDocs-only change; no code touched. Workspace unaffected (last full run: 759 passed / 0 failed, clippy clean).",
