    {
      "id": "d19bdbe7-a355-4c64-923e-d3f48af6db19",
      "phaseId": "1df9c36c-5c29-4288-9fe1-7a6e9c72179b",
      "number": 278,
      "shortId": "SNEKU",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "choice-1-choice-widget-value-c",
      "title": "choice-1: `Choice` widget — value-carrying, content-composable option primitive",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Build the **`Choice`** widget: a selectable container that carries a value and composes arbitrary content as children. The option primitive `Select`/`Tabs` (later `ContextMenu`/`CommandPalette`) mount.\n\n## STATUS: code complete on `feat/viewnode-button-composition` (uncommitted). AWAITING USER TEST → then commit.\n\n## IMPLEMENTED\n**`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/choice.rs` (new)**\n- `Choice::new(value)` (no content) / `Choice::labeled(value, label)` (sugar → one `Label` child — the same child a caller would compose; one content model, no \"simple mode\").\n- `impl Parent` (`.child(any Component)`), `impl LayoutExt`, embeds `Base`.\n- `.selected(bool)` / `.state() -> Signal<bool>` / `.hovered()` / `.value() -> &str` / `.on_activate(f)` (click / Enter / Space; sets `base.focusable`).\n- **Chrome only**: selected pill (`accent` @ `interaction.row_active_fill`), hover tint (`foreground` @ `row_hover_fill`), press `Flash`, focus ring — the SAME interaction tokens as `Item`, so an option and a list row read as one family.\n- **State color published** via `cx.with_content_color(selected ? accent : foreground)` around the children paint → unstyled `Label`/`Icon` children tint with the selection; a child with its own color keeps it.\n- `base.focus_barrier = true` — one option = one Tab stop.\n- `remeasure` **hugs content**: `width`/`height` = `Auto`, `padding = BASE_PAD(8.0) * pad_scale`, `gap = font * 0.5` (same half-character rhythm as `Button`). No char-count arithmetic; the size variant cascades into the content automatically.\n- `tick` recurses into children.\n- **`pub fn choice_at(&[Box<dyn Component>], Point) -> Option<usize>`** — resolves a pick from the children's **real bounds**. Exported so `Select`/`Tabs` (choice-2/3) resolve picks from bounds, never row arithmetic: what is drawn and what is clickable can never disagree.\n\n## DECISION RECORDED — the value type is a plain `String`\n`heca-grid-ui` must never depend on `heca` (AGENTS.md ⛔ SETTLED), so the widget cannot store the app's `PropValue`. A plain `String` is the one shape both sides speak; the host converts to/from richer types at its boundary (choice-4 maps the node's `value` prop → this string, and back when dispatching the change intent). Rejected the grid-ui-local `ChoiceValue{Text,Int}` enum — no consumer needs numeric fidelity, and it would duplicate `PropValue` in the library.\n\n## Exports / docs / demo\n- `widgets/mod.rs` (`mod choice;` + `pub use choice::{choice_at, Choice}`), `lib.rs` root export + prelude.\n- Showcase: new \"Choice — a value + composed content (the option primitive)\" row — a text option, a selected icon+label option, and a two-line option with a sub-label.\n- `docs/widgets.md`: full `Choice` entry (every builder/accessor, the chrome, the bounds-picking rule) + **the `Choice` vs `Item` comparison table + rule of thumb** (the guidance the user asked for; choice-8 will cross-link it), + TOC. Declarative form noted as landing in choice-4.\n- Rustdoc: exhaustive, incl. the `Choice` vs `Item` table.\n\n## Tests (+4, `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs`)\n`choice_carries_a_value_and_composes_its_content` (value independent of content; sugar == composed; empty is legal) · `choice_content_inherits_the_selected_state_color` (selected → accent, unselected → foreground, explicit child color wins) · `a_choice_is_one_tab_stop_whatever_it_contains` (with an interactive child inside) · `choice_at_resolves_a_pick_from_real_bounds`.\n\n## GATES (2026-07-13)\nheca-grid-ui 134 + 71 + 1 green (was 130); workspace builds; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` clean (only the pre-existing transitive `block v0.1.6` note); showcase builds.\n\n## NEXT\nUser tests the showcase (hover/select the Choice row; the selected one's icon+label should tint together) → commit → **choice-2** (`Select` onto `Choice` children — the fiddly overlay/bounds one).\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDONE 2026-07-13 — commit `e7af2c9`, pushed to `feat/viewnode-button-composition` (PR #237 → main). User approved.\n\n## Shipped\n**`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/choice.rs` (NEW)** — the option primitive: a selectable container carrying a **value** and composing **arbitrary content** as children.\n- `Choice::new(value)` (no content) / `Choice::labeled(value, label)` (sugar → one `Label` child — the same child a caller composes by hand; one content model, no \"simple mode\").\n- `impl Parent` (`.child(any Component)`) + `impl LayoutExt`; `.selected(bool)` / `.state() -> Signal<bool>` / `.hovered()` / `.value() -> &str` / `.on_activate(f)` (click / Enter / Space; sets `base.focusable`).\n- **Chrome only**: selected pill (`accent` @ `interaction.row_active_fill`), hover tint (`foreground` @ `row_hover_fill`), press `Flash`, focus ring — the **same interaction tokens as `Item`**, so an option and a list row read as one family.\n- **State color published** via `cx.with_content_color(selected ? accent : foreground)` around the children paint → a selected option's `Icon` + `Label` tint **together**, with neither knowing about selection. A child with its own color (e.g. `Badge::danger`) keeps it.\n- `base.focus_barrier = true` — one option = one Tab stop, whatever it composes.\n- `remeasure` **hugs content**: `width`/`height` = `Auto`, `padding = BASE_PAD(8.0) * pad_scale`, `gap = font * 0.5` (the same half-character rhythm as `Button`). No char-count arithmetic; the size variant cascades into the content automatically.\n- `tick` recurses into children.\n- **`pub fn choice_at(&[Box<dyn Component>], Point) -> Option<usize>`** — resolves a pick from the children's **REAL BOUNDS**. Exported specifically so choice-2/3 cannot fall back to row arithmetic; the invariant is **bounds === what is drawn === what is clickable**.\n\n## DECISION RECORDED — the value is a plain `String`\n`heca-grid-ui` never depends on `heca` (AGENTS.md ⛔ SETTLED), so the widget cannot store the app's `PropValue`. A `String` is the one shape both sides speak; `realize` converts at the boundary (choice-4 maps the node's `value` prop → this string, and back when dispatching the change intent). A grid-ui-local `ChoiceValue{Text,Int}` enum was **rejected** — no consumer needs numeric fidelity, and it would duplicate `PropValue` inside the library.\n\n## Also\n- Exports: `widgets/mod.rs` (`mod choice;` + `pub use choice::{choice_at, Choice}`), `lib.rs` root + prelude.\n- Showcase: \"Choice — a value + composed content (the option primitive)\" row — a text option, a **selected** icon+label option, and a two-line option with a sub-label.\n- `docs/widgets.md`: full `Choice` entry (every builder/accessor, the chrome, the bounds-picking rule) **+ the `Choice` vs `Item` comparison table and rule of thumb** — the guidance the user asked for (rows that look like rows → `Item`; picking one of several → `Choice`). choice-8 will cross-link it. TOC updated. Declarative form (`WidgetKind::Choice`) noted as landing in choice-4.\n- Rustdoc: exhaustive, including the `Choice` vs `Item` table.\n\n## Tests (+4, `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs`)\n`choice_carries_a_value_and_composes_its_content` · `choice_content_inherits_the_selected_state_color` (selected → accent, unselected → foreground, explicit child color wins) · `a_choice_is_one_tab_stop_whatever_it_contains` (with an interactive child inside) · `choice_at_resolves_a_pick_from_real_bounds`.\n\n## Gates\nheca-grid-ui **134** + 71 + 1 green (was 130); workspace builds; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` clean (only the pre-existing transitive `block v0.1.6` note); showcase builds.\n\n## NEXT\n**choice-2** (`6ec99b20`) — refactor `Select` onto `Choice` children. The fiddly one: its dropdown paints on the overlay layer but hit-tests rows by arithmetic; the options must become children whose bounds are real *inside the overlay panel* (fallback documented in that task: bake the panel offset into the children's bounds, as `ScrollRegion` does with its scroll offset).",
